n/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Where are the exact rules for a challenge?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On that challenge's page. It is the source of truth for the task, deadline, prize, scoring, benchmark, budget, eligibility, revision limit and submission format."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does every entry get the same test?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Every entry inside a challenge is evaluated under the same published scoring method and execution rules. The inputs may be hidden, live or randomly selected when the challenge page says so."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to publish my code?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not unless the challenge says so. The submission page states whether public repositories, private read-only access or hosted endpoints are accepted. Never commit secrets to a repository."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who owns submitted work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You keep ownership unless separate written terms are agreed before entry. A prize, certificate or public result does not silently transfer ownership."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a result be disqualified?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, for a stated rule violation, fabricated evidence, evaluator tampering, malicious code, identity abuse or other clear bad faith. A low score, simple approach or honest failure is not a disqualification."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When is a winner final?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Leaderboard positions are provisional until the exact submitted artifact passes the verification stated on the challenge page. If it cannot be reproduced or audited, the entry is prize-ineligible and the next eligible entry moves up—or the prize remains unawarded—under that challenge's policy."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What if nobody clears the bar?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Builderr does not force a winner. If no entry clears the published qualification bar, the challenge page's rollover or return policy applies."}}]}</script><p class="mb-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--accent-ink)]">Rules</p><h1 class="max-w-[760px] text-4xl font-semibold leading-[1.05] tracking-[-.04em] md:text-5xl">One short rulebook. Exact rules on each challenge.</h1><p class="mt-5 max-w-[720px] text-lg leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">These rules apply across Builderr. Each challenge page is the source of truth for its task, deadline, prize, scoring, benchmark, budget, eligibility, revisions and submission format.</p><div class="mt-7 flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-center"><a class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center justify-center rounded-md bg-[var(--accent)] px-5 py-3 font-medium" style="color:#fff" href="/#challenges">View open challenges →</a><a class="font-medium" href="/start">How to enter</a></div><section class="mt-14 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-10" aria-labelledby="shared-rules"><p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--accent-ink)]">Platform-wide</p><h2 id="shared-rules" class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-.03em]">Rules shared by every challenge</h2><div class="mt-7 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-7 sm:grid-cols-2"><div class="border-t-2 border-[var(--accent)] pt-3"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--accent-ink)]">01</span><h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold">The challenge page controls</h3><p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">Read it before building. If a global summary conflicts with the challenge page, the challenge page wins.</p></div><div class="border-t-2 border-[var(--accent)] pt-3"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--accent-ink)]">02</span><h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold">Same method inside each challenge</h3><p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">Entries use the same published scoring method, execution rules and minimum requirements for that challenge.</p></div><div class="border-t-2 border-[var(--accent)] pt-3"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--accent-ink)]">03</span><h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold">Submit an exact version</h3><p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">Provide the repository, commit, artifact or endpoint requested. The evaluated version—not a later replacement—is the entry of record.</p></div><div class="border-t-2 border-[var(--accent)] pt-3"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--accent-ink)]">04</span><h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold">Stay inside the stated boundaries</h3><p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">Respect the data, network, runtime, cost, model, source and revision limits listed on the challenge page.</p></div><div class="border-t-2 border-[var(--accent)] pt-3"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--accent-ink)]">05</span><h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold">Show honest evidence</h3><p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">Do not fabricate outputs, sources, runs or claims. Missing evidence should remain missing rather than being guessed.</p></div><div class="border-t-2 border-[var(--accent)] pt-3"><span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--accent-ink)]">06</span><h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold">Results are provisional until verified</h3><p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">A leaderboard can update quickly. A prize, winner status or certificate requires the exact verification stated for that challenge.</p></div></div></section><section class="mt-14 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-10" aria-labelledby="challenge-rules"><p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--accent-ink)]">Exact scoring</p><h2 id="challenge-rules" class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-.03em]">Rules for each challenge</h2><p class="mt-3 max-w-[700px] leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">2<!-- --> challenges are listed as open, with $<!-- -->3,500<!-- --> in prizes. Use the relevant page below for the complete, current rules.</p><div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2"><article id="signalpost-rules" class="scroll-mt-36 rounded-xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--card)] p-5"><p class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--accent-ink)]">Open challenge<!-- --> · <!-- -->$2,500</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold">Signalpost company research</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">Build an agent that finds company information online.</p><a class="mt-4 inline-block font-medium" href="/challenges/signalpost#scoring">Read Signalpost scoring<!-- --> →</a></article><article id="trading-rules" class="scroll-mt-36 rounded-xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--card)] p-5"><p class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--accent-ink)]">Open challenge<!-- --> · <!-- -->$1,000</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold">Trading agents</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">Build a trading agent that buys and sells US stocks with paper money.</p><a class="mt-4 inline-block font-medium" href="/trading-v0#rules">Read Trading rules<!-- --> →</a></article><article id="video-rules" class="scroll-mt-36 rounded-xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--card)] p-5"><p class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--accent-ink)]">Published deadline passed<!-- --> · <!-- -->$300</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold">Kitchen CCTV monitor</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">Build an agent that watches kitchen video and answers questions about what happened.</p><a class="mt-4 inline-block font-medium" href="/kitchen-video#scoring">Read Kitchen CCTV scoring<!-- --> →</a></article><article id="stt-rules" class="scroll-mt-36 rounded-xl border border-[var(--border)] bg-[var(--card)] p-5"><p class="text-[10px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--accent-ink)]">Past result<!-- --> · <!-- -->$500</p><h3 class="mt-2 text-xl font-semibold">Local dictation</h3><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">Build a local dictation tool that turns Hindi+English speech into text. Round 1 is complete.</p><a class="mt-4 inline-block font-medium" href="/speech-to-text#scoring">View Local dictation result<!-- --> →</a></article></div></section><section class="mt-14 grid gap-8 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-10 md:grid-cols-2" aria-label="Fairness and ownership"><div><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What can invalidate an entry</h2><ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]"><li>Failing a mandatory requirement or breaking an explicit rule on the challenge page.</li><li>Using forbidden information, evaluator internals or another entrant&#x27;s private work.</li><li>Fabricating evidence, results, identities or eligibility.</li><li>Malicious code, credential access, evaluator tampering or deliberate service abuse.</li></ul><p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">A low score, simple approach, honest bug or failed experiment is not misconduct. Builderr states the issue and gives the builder a chance to respond before a final discretionary call.</p></div><div><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Code, privacy and ownership</h2><ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]"><li>Never commit API keys, passwords or private data.</li><li>Builderr uses submitted access under the challenge’s published evaluation, verification and sharing terms.</li><li>You keep ownership unless separate written licensing or transfer terms were agreed before entry.</li><li>Public result pages distinguish measured facts from private or unavailable artifacts.</li></ul></div></section><section class="mt-14 rounded-xl border border-[var(--accent)] bg-[var(--white-band)] p-6 md:p-8" aria-labelledby="winner-verification"><p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--accent-ink)]">Before payment</p><h2 id="winner-verification" class="text-2xl font-semibold">Winner verification</h2><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">For challenges that require an exact scored agent, a provisional winner must provide read-only access to that exact agent version. Builderr checks reproducibility, eligibility and material rule compliance before issuing a prize, winner status, or certificate. An entry that cannot be reproduced or audited is prize-ineligible, and the next eligible entry moves up—or the prize remains unawarded— under that challenge&#x27;s published policy.</p></section><section class="mt-14 border-t border-[var(--border)] pt-10" aria-labelledby="rules-faq"><h2 id="rules-faq" class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-[-.03em]">FAQ</h2><div class="mt-4"><details class="group border-b border-[var(--border)] last:border-0"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-4 font-semibold transition-colors hover:text-[var(--accent-ink)] [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><span>Where are the exact rules for a challenge?</span><span class="shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-[var(--accent-ink)] transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="pb-5 pr-8 leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">On that challenge&#x27;s page. It is the source of truth for the task, deadline, prize, scoring, benchmark, budget, eligibility, revision limit and submission format.</p></details><details class="group border-b border-[var(--border)] last:border-0"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-4 font-semibold transition-colors hover:text-[var(--accent-ink)] [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><span>Does every entry get the same test?</span><span class="shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-[var(--accent-ink)] transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="pb-5 pr-8 leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">Every entry inside a challenge is evaluated under the same published scoring method and execution rules. The inputs may be hidden, live or randomly selected when the challenge page says so.</p></details><details class="group border-b border-[var(--border)] last:border-0"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-4 font-semibold transition-colors hover:text-[var(--accent-ink)] [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><span>Do I have to publish my code?</span><span class="shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-[var(--accent-ink)] transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="pb-5 pr-8 leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">Not unless the challenge says so. The submission page states whether public repositories, private read-only access or hosted endpoints are accepted. Never commit secrets to a repository.</p></details><details class="group border-b border-[var(--border)] last:border-0"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-4 font-semibold transition-colors hover:text-[var(--accent-ink)] [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><span>Who owns submitted work?</span><span class="shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-[var(--accent-ink)] transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="pb-5 pr-8 leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">You keep ownership unless separate written terms are agreed before entry. A prize, certificate or public result does not silently transfer ownership.</p></details><details class="group border-b border-[var(--border)] last:border-0"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 py-4 font-semibold transition-colors hover:text-[var(--accent-ink)] [&amp;::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden"><span>Can a result be disqualified?</span><span class="shrink-0 text-xl leading-none text-[var(--accent-ink)] transition-transform group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p